  summary: "Unemployment describes people who are employable and actively seeking work but cannot find it; it may be voluntary (jobless by choice) or involuntary (excluded from a failing economy), and it is measured by the unemployment rate. Its effects cascade from family hardship to weak demand, lower profits and government budget cuts. The solutions are creating adequate and fairly paid jobs, encouraging diverse career choices, and pursuing sustainable development, whose four intertwined dimensions ultimately deliver sustainable employment.",
